{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788164258574,"sessionID":"ses_fa923204fffeJOVYIIzNA2JDJK","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_2e38f82e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.opencode/commands/security-review-ref.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.opencode/commands/security-review-ref.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Security Review — Classification & Format Reference\n2: \n3: This file is the reference specification for `/security-review`. It is read by\n4: `@critic` and `@verifier` subagents, and by the primary agent during step 6\n5: (scan and classify). Do NOT execute this file — it contains no steps.\n6: \n7: ## Prohibited actions\n8: \n9: - Do NOT invent CWE numbers outside the list below.\n10: - Do NOT invent CVE IDs.\n11: - Do NOT add fields to the finding format.\n12: - Do NOT omit fields from the finding format.\n13: - Do NOT create new sections beyond those in the report structure.\n14: - Do NOT write findings for clean files. Move on silently.\n15: - Do NOT manufacture findings to fill empty sections. Write \"None\".\n16: - Do NOT re-classify DEAD code as ACTIVE without a verified call chain.\n17: - Do NOT assign Confidence CONFIRMED without file:line at every trace hop.\n18: - Do NOT write narrative prose in findings. Use the format exactly.\n19: \n20: ## Classification system\n21: \n22: Every finding MUST be classified on four independent axes. Pick exactly one\n23: value per axis. Do not collapse axes. Do not invent values.\n24: \n25: ### Reachability\n26: \n27: Determine reachability FIRST, before assessing Impact or Likelihood.\n28: \n29: - **ACTIVE** — Called from an entry point listed in `## Attack surface`.\n30:   Requires a concrete call chain: entry point -> intermediate calls -> this\n31:   code, with file:line at each hop. If you cannot write the chain, it is\n32:   NOT ACTIVE. Do not guess. Do not infer.\n33: - **CONDITIONAL** — Reachable only when a named condition is true. State\n34:   the exact condition (e.g., \"DEBUG=true in .env\", \"feature flag X enabled\").\n35:   Condition off by default: set Likelihood to LOW. On by default: no effect.\n36: - **DEAD** — No call path from any entry point. Orphaned functions,\n37:   unreferenced modules, commented-out code. Verify: grep for the function\n38:   name across the codebase. Zero call sites outside its own file = DEAD.\n39:   Report under `## Dead code findings`. Do not re-classify as ACTIVE later\n40:   unless the critic provides a verified call chain.\n41: - **TEST-ONLY** — Called only from test files (`test_*`, `*_test`, `/tests/`).\n42:   Report under `## Test-only findings`. Severity capped at LOW unless the\n43:   test server is exposed to a network. Do not treat as ACTIVE.\n44: \n45: ### Impact (damage if exploited)\n46: \n47: - **CRITICAL** — Full system compromise: RCE, complete auth bypass, full\n48:   database dump, persistent backdoor, cryptographic key extraction.\n49: - **HIGH** — Significant damage: privilege escalation, bulk data exposure\n50:   (PII, credentials, financial), persistent injection (stored XSS), secret\n51:   exposure, arbitrary file read/write.\n52: - **MODERATE** — Contained damage: single-user data exposure, session hijack,\n53:   partial access control bypass, CSRF on state-changing actions.\n54: - **LOW** — Minimal damage: version/path info disclosure, verbose error\n55:   messages, denial of service, defense-in-depth gaps, missing security headers.\n56: \n57: ### Likelihood (feasibility of exploitation)\n58: \n59: - **HIGH** — All of: unauthenticated, publicly reachable, no special\n60:   conditions, well-known exploit pattern, single-step attack.\n61: - **MEDIUM** — Any one of: requires authentication, requires one specific\n62:   precondition, requires a 2-step attack chain.\n63: - **LOW** — Two or more of: requires privileged/admin access, requires\n64:   specific configuration, requires 3+ step chain, race condition, or social\n65:   engineering.\n66: \n67: ### Confidence (certainty this is real)\n68: \n69: - **CONFIRMED** — Full source-to-sink trace verified by reading actual code.\n70:   Every hop cites a real file:line that was read.\n71: - **PROBABLE** — Trace mostly verified but one hop is inferred. State which\n72:   hop is inferred.\n73: - **POSSIBLE** — Vulnerable pattern detected but data flow from untrusted\n74:   source to sink is not confirmed. Input might be hardcoded, sanitized\n75:   upstream, or unreachable.\n76: \n77: ### Severity (derived — do NOT assign directly)\n78: \n79: Look up Impact x Likelihood in this matrix:\n80: \n81: |                     | Likelihood HIGH | Likelihood MEDIUM | Likelihood LOW |\n82: |---------------------|-----------------|-------------------|----------------|\n83: | **Impact CRITICAL** | CRITICAL        | HIGH              | MEDIUM         |\n84: | **Impact HIGH**     | HIGH            | HIGH              | MEDIUM         |\n85: | **Impact MODERATE** | MEDIUM          | MEDIUM            | LOW            |\n86: | **Impact LOW**      | LOW             | LOW               | LOW            |\n87: \n88: Reachability adjustments (applied after matrix lookup):\n89: - **ACTIVE**: no change.\n90: - **CONDITIONAL**: no change, but condition MUST be reflected in Likelihood.\n91: - **DEAD**: cap at MEDIUM. Note \"(capped from [original] — dead code)\".\n92: - **TEST-ONLY**: cap at LOW. Note \"(capped from [original] — test-only)\".\n93: \n94: Show the computation in every finding:\n95: `Severity: Impact [X] x Likelihood [Y] = [Z] ([reachability], [adjustment])`\n96: \n97: ## Rules for classification\n98: \n99: These rules are hard constraints. Do not override them with reasoning.\n100: \n101: - No trace = not CONFIRMED. If you cannot write source -> sink with file:line\n102:   at every hop, set Confidence to POSSIBLE. No exceptions.\n103: - Dead code: report it, classify as DEAD, cap severity at MEDIUM. Do NOT\n104:   skip dead code. Do NOT inflate dead code to ACTIVE.\n105: - Full mitigation = no finding. If a mitigation fully neutralizes the\n106:   vulnerability, do NOT report it. Do NOT report it as \"mitigated\" either.\n107:   Partial mitigation (e.g., blocklist not allowlist): report it, lower\n108:   Likelihood by one level.\n109: - Clean files: move on silently. Do NOT write \"no findings\" entries. Do NOT\n110:   mention clean files anywhere in the assessment.\n111: - Clean codebase: write `## Findings\\nNo vulnerabilities found.` Do NOT\n112:   lower standards to fill the section. An empty findings section with \"No\n113:   vulnerabilities found\" is a valid review outcome.\n114: \n115: ## CWE list (use ONLY these)\n116: \n117: CWE-22 Path Traversal | CWE-78 Command Injection | CWE-79 XSS | CWE-89 SQLi |\n118: CWE-94 Code Injection | CWE-200 Info Exposure | CWE-259 Hardcoded Password |\n119: CWE-284 Access Control | CWE-306 Missing Auth | CWE-327 Broken Crypto |\n120: CWE-352 CSRF | CWE-400 Resource Exhaustion | CWE-502 Unsafe Deserialization |\n121: CWE-611 XXE | CWE-918 SSRF | CWE-OTHER (describe)\n122: \n123: No invented CVE IDs. No CWE numbers outside this list.\n124: \n125: ## Finding format — first-party code\n126: \n127: ```markdown\n128: ### [FILE]:[LINES] — [TITLE]\n129: **CWE:** CWE-XXX\n130: **Reachability:** [exactly one of: ACTIVE | CONDITIONAL | DEAD | TEST-ONLY]\n131: **Impact:** [exactly one of: CRITICAL | HIGH | MODERATE | LOW]\n132: **Likelihood:** [exactly one of: HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW]\n133: **Confidence:** [exactly one of: CONFIRMED | PROBABLE | POSSIBLE]\n134: **Severity:** Impact [X] x Likelihood [Y] = [Z] ([reachability], [adjustment])\n135: \n136: **Data flow:**\n137: Source:     [file:line — what untrusted data enters here]\n138: Transform:  [file:line — function/method, what it does to the data]\n139: Transform:  [file:line — next hop, if any]\n140: Sink:       [file:line — where the data causes harm]\n141: \n142: \\`\\`\\`python\n143: <exact code at the sink, max 20 lines, copied verbatim from the file>\n144: \\`\\`\\`\n145: \n146: **Exploit:** 1. [concrete attacker action] -> 2. [how input reaches sink] -> 3. [resulting harm]\n147: **Mitigations:** [existing controls and whether sufficient, or \"None\"]\n148: **Fix:** [specific code change recommendation]\n149: ```\n150: \n151: Use this format exactly. Do not omit fields. Do not add fields.\n152: \n153: ## Finding format — dependency findings\n154: \n155: ```markdown\n156: ### [PACKAGE]@[VERSION] — [TITLE]\n157: **CVE:** [CVE-XXXX-XXXXX or \"no CVE — advisory only\"]\n158: **CWE:** CWE-XXX\n159: **Reachability:** [ACTIVE — vulnerable function called at file:line | DEAD — not imported/called]\n160: **Impact:** [exactly one of: CRITICAL | HIGH | MODERATE | LOW]\n161: **Likelihood:** [exactly one of: HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW]\n162: **Confidence:** [exactly one of: CONFIRMED | PROBABLE | POSSIBLE]\n163: **Severity:** Impact [X] x Likelihood [Y] = [Z] ([reachability], [adjustment])\n164: \n165: **Vulnerable path:** [import chain -> function at file:line, or \"not called in codebase\"]\n166: **Fixed in:** [version, or \"no fix available\"]\n167: **Fix:** [upgrade | pin | remove | workaround]\n168: ```\n169: \n170: Use this format exactly. Do not omit fields. Do not add fields.\n171: \n172: ## Report structure\n173: \n174: The assessment file MUST contain these sections in this order. Write empty\n175: sections (with \"None\" or \"No findings\") rather than omitting them.\n176: \n177: 1. `# Security Assessment — [date] — [model]`\n178: 2. `## Context` (project, framework, deployment, ports, auth, data stores)\n179: 3. `## Attack surface` (entry points + trust boundaries tables)\n180: 4. `## Scanned files` (file list)\n181: 4. `## Findings` (ACTIVE and CONDITIONAL, ordered by severity descending)\n182: 5. `## Dead code findings` (DEAD, severity capped at MEDIUM)\n183: 6. `## Test-only findings` (TEST-ONLY, severity capped at LOW)\n184: 7. `## Dependency findings` (third-party/supply-chain)\n185: 8. `## Findings summary` (tables below)\n186: 9. `## Disputed findings` (after critic review; \"None\" if no disputes)\n187: 10. `## Validation` (after subagent review)\n188: 11. `## Run metadata` (model, date, finding counts, critic/verifier status)\n189: \n190: ## Findings summary tables\n191: \n192: ### First-party code\n193: Total findings: X (Active: X, Conditional: X, Dead: X, Test-only: X)\n194: \n195: | Severity | Count | Confirmed | Probable | Possible |\n196: |----------|-------|-----------|----------|----------|\n197: | CRITICAL | X     | X         | X        | X        |\n198: | HIGH     | X     | X         | X        | X        |\n199: | MEDIUM   | X     | X         | X        | X        |\n200: | LOW      | X     | X         | X        | X        |\n201: \n202: ### Dependencies\n203: Total findings: X (Active: X, Dead: X)\n204: \n205: | Package | Version | CVE | Severity | Called? |\n206: |---------|---------|-----|----------|---------|\n207: \n208: ### All findings\n209: \n210: | File/Package | Finding | CWE | Reachability | Impact | Likelihood | Severity | Confidence |\n211: |--------------|---------|-----|--------------|--------|------------|----------|------------|\n\n(End of file - total 211 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Security Review — Classification & Format Reference\n\nThis file is the reference specification for `/security-review`. It is read by\n`@critic` and `@verifier` subagents, and by the primary agent during step 6\n(scan and classify). Do NOT execute this file — it contains no steps.\n\n## Prohibited actions\n\n- Do NOT invent CWE numbers outside the list below.\n- Do NOT invent CVE IDs.\n- Do NOT add fields to the finding format.\n- Do NOT omit fields from the finding format.\n- Do NOT create new sections beyond those in the report structure.\n- Do NOT write findings for clean files. Move on silently.\n- Do NOT manufacture findings to fill empty sections. Write \"None\".\n- Do NOT re-classify DEAD code as ACTIVE without a verified call chain.\n- Do NOT assign Confidence CONFIRMED without file:line at every trace hop.\n- Do NOT write narrative prose in findings. Use the format exactly.\n\n## Classification system","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.opencode/commands/security-review-ref.md","text":"# Security Review — Classification & Format Reference\n\nThis file is the reference specification for `/security-review`. It is read by\n`@critic` and `@verifier` subagents, and by the primary agent during step 6\n(scan and classify). Do NOT execute this file — it contains no steps.\n\n## Prohibited actions\n\n- Do NOT invent CWE numbers outside the list below.\n- Do NOT invent CVE IDs.\n- Do NOT add fields to the finding format.\n- Do NOT omit fields from the finding format.\n- Do NOT create new sections beyond those in the report structure.\n- Do NOT write findings for clean files. Move on silently.\n- Do NOT manufacture findings to fill empty sections. Write \"None\".\n- Do NOT re-classify DEAD code as ACTIVE without a verified call chain.\n- Do NOT assign Confidence CONFIRMED without file:line at every trace hop.\n- Do NOT write narrative prose in findings. Use the format exactly.\n\n## Classification system\n\nEvery finding MUST be classified on four independent axes. Pick exactly one\nvalue per axis. Do not collapse axes. Do not invent values.\n\n### Reachability\n\nDetermine reachability FIRST, before assessing Impact or Likelihood.\n\n- **ACTIVE** — Called from an entry point listed in `## Attack surface`.\n  Requires a concrete call chain: entry point -> intermediate calls -> this\n  code, with file:line at each hop. If you cannot write the chain, it is\n  NOT ACTIVE. Do not guess. Do not infer.\n- **CONDITIONAL** — Reachable only when a named condition is true. State\n  the exact condition (e.g., \"DEBUG=true in .env\", \"feature flag X enabled\").\n  Condition off by default: set Likelihood to LOW. On by default: no effect.\n- **DEAD** — No call path from any entry point. Orphaned functions,\n  unreferenced modules, commented-out code. Verify: grep for the function\n  name across the codebase. Zero call sites outside its own file = DEAD.\n  Report under `## Dead code findings`. Do not re-classify as ACTIVE later\n  unless the critic provides a verified call chain.\n- **TEST-ONLY** — Called only from test files (`test_*`, `*_test`, `/tests/`).\n  Report under `## Test-only findings`. Severity capped at LOW unless the\n  test server is exposed to a network. Do not treat as ACTIVE.\n\n### Impact (damage if exploited)\n\n- **CRITICAL** — Full system compromise: RCE, complete auth bypass, full\n  database dump, persistent backdoor, cryptographic key extraction.\n- **HIGH** — Significant damage: privilege escalation, bulk data exposure\n  (PII, credentials, financial), persistent injection (stored XSS), secret\n  exposure, arbitrary file read/write.\n- **MODERATE** — Contained damage: single-user data exposure, session hijack,\n  partial access control bypass, CSRF on state-changing actions.\n- **LOW** — Minimal damage: version/path info disclosure, verbose error\n  messages, denial of service, defense-in-depth gaps, missing security headers.\n\n### Likelihood (feasibility of exploitation)\n\n- **HIGH** — All of: unauthenticated, publicly reachable, no special\n  conditions, well-known exploit pattern, single-step attack.\n- **MEDIUM** — Any one of: requires authentication, requires one specific\n  precondition, requires a 2-step attack chain.\n- **LOW** — Two or more of: requires privileged/admin access, requires\n  specific configuration, requires 3+ step chain, race condition, or social\n  engineering.\n\n### Confidence (certainty this is real)\n\n- **CONFIRMED** — Full source-to-sink trace verified by reading actual code.\n  Every hop cites a real file:line that was read.\n- **PROBABLE** — Trace mostly verified but one hop is inferred. State which\n  hop is inferred.\n- **POSSIBLE** — Vulnerable pattern detected but data flow from untrusted\n  source to sink is not confirmed. Input might be hardcoded, sanitized\n  upstream, or unreachable.\n\n### Severity (derived — do NOT assign directly)\n\nLook up Impact x Likelihood in this matrix:\n\n|                     | Likelihood HIGH | Likelihood MEDIUM | Likelihood LOW |\n|---------------------|-----------------|-------------------|----------------|\n| **Impact CRITICAL** | CRITICAL        | HIGH              | MEDIUM         |\n| **Impact HIGH**     | HIGH            | HIGH              | MEDIUM         |\n| **Impact MODERATE** | MEDIUM          | MEDIUM            | LOW            |\n| **Impact LOW**      | LOW             | LOW               | LOW            |\n\nReachability adjustments (applied after matrix lookup):\n- **ACTIVE**: no change.\n- **CONDITIONAL**: no change, but condition MUST be reflected in Likelihood.\n- **DEAD**: cap at MEDIUM. Note \"(capped from [original] — dead code)\".\n- **TEST-ONLY**: cap at LOW. Note \"(capped from [original] — test-only)\".\n\nShow the computation in every finding:\n`Severity: Impact [X] x Likelihood [Y] = [Z] ([reachability], [adjustment])`\n\n## Rules for classification\n\nThese rules are hard constraints. Do not override them with reasoning.\n\n- No trace = not CONFIRMED. If you cannot write source -> sink with file:line\n  at every hop, set Confidence to POSSIBLE. No exceptions.\n- Dead code: report it, classify as DEAD, cap severity at MEDIUM. Do NOT\n  skip dead code. Do NOT inflate dead code to ACTIVE.\n- Full mitigation = no finding. If a mitigation fully neutralizes the\n  vulnerability, do NOT report it. Do NOT report it as \"mitigated\" either.\n  Partial mitigation (e.g., blocklist not allowlist): report it, lower\n  Likelihood by one level.\n- Clean files: move on silently. Do NOT write \"no findings\" entries. Do NOT\n  mention clean files anywhere in the assessment.\n- Clean codebase: write `## Findings\\nNo vulnerabilities found.` Do NOT\n  lower standards to fill the section. An empty findings section with \"No\n  vulnerabilities found\" is a valid review outcome.\n\n## CWE list (use ONLY these)\n\nCWE-22 Path Traversal | CWE-78 Command Injection | CWE-79 XSS | CWE-89 SQLi |\nCWE-94 Code Injection | CWE-200 Info Exposure | CWE-259 Hardcoded Password |\nCWE-284 Access Control | CWE-306 Missing Auth | CWE-327 Broken Crypto |\nCWE-352 CSRF | CWE-400 Resource Exhaustion | CWE-502 Unsafe Deserialization |\nCWE-611 XXE | CWE-918 SSRF | CWE-OTHER (describe)\n\nNo invented CVE IDs. No CWE numbers outside this list.\n\n## Finding format — first-party code\n\n```markdown\n### [FILE]:[LINES] — [TITLE]\n**CWE:** CWE-XXX\n**Reachability:** [exactly one of: ACTIVE | CONDITIONAL | DEAD | TEST-ONLY]\n**Impact:** [exactly one of: CRITICAL | HIGH | MODERATE | LOW]\n**Likelihood:** [exactly one of: HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW]\n**Confidence:** [exactly one of: CONFIRMED | PROBABLE | POSSIBLE]\n**Severity:** Impact [X] x Likelihood [Y] = [Z] ([reachability], [adjustment])\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     [file:line — what untrusted data enters here]\nTransform:  [file:line — function/method, what it does to the data]\nTransform:  [file:line — next hop, if any]\nSink:       [file:line — where the data causes harm]\n\n\\`\\`\\`python\n<exact code at the sink, max 20 lines, copied verbatim from the file>\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n**Exploit:** 1. [concrete attacker action] -> 2. [how input reaches sink] -> 3. [resulting harm]\n**Mitigations:** [existing controls and whether sufficient, or \"None\"]\n**Fix:** [specific code change recommendation]\n```\n\nUse this format exactly. Do not omit fields. Do not add fields.\n\n## Finding format — dependency findings\n\n```markdown\n### [PACKAGE]@[VERSION] — [TITLE]\n**CVE:** [CVE-XXXX-XXXXX or \"no CVE — advisory only\"]\n**CWE:** CWE-XXX\n**Reachability:** [ACTIVE — vulnerable function called at file:line | DEAD — not imported/called]\n**Impact:** [exactly one of: CRITICAL | HIGH | MODERATE | LOW]\n**Likelihood:** [exactly one of: HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW]\n**Confidence:** [exactly one of: CONFIRMED | PROBABLE | POSSIBLE]\n**Severity:** Impact [X] x Likelihood [Y] = [Z] ([reachability], [adjustment])\n\n**Vulnerable path:** [import chain -> function at file:line, or \"not called in codebase\"]\n**Fixed in:** [version, or \"no fix available\"]\n**Fix:** [upgrade | pin | remove | workaround]\n```\n\nUse this format exactly. Do not omit fields. Do not add fields.\n\n## Report structure\n\nThe assessment file MUST contain these sections in this order. Write empty\nsections (with \"None\" or \"No findings\") rather than omitting them.\n\n1. `# Security Assessment — [date] — [model]`\n2. `## Context` (project, framework, deployment, ports, auth, data stores)\n3. `## Attack surface` (entry points + trust boundaries tables)\n4. `## Scanned files` (file list)\n4. `## Findings` (ACTIVE and CONDITIONAL, ordered by severity descending)\n5. `## Dead code findings` (DEAD, severity capped at MEDIUM)\n6. `## Test-only findings` (TEST-ONLY, severity capped at LOW)\n7. `## Dependency findings` (third-party/supply-chain)\n8. `## Findings summary` (tables below)\n9. `## Disputed findings` (after critic review; \"None\" if no disputes)\n10. `## Validation` (after subagent review)\n11. `## Run metadata` (model, date, finding counts, critic/verifier status)\n\n## Findings summary tables\n\n### First-party code\nTotal findings: X (Active: X, Conditional: X, Dead: X, Test-only: X)\n\n| Severity | Count | Confirmed | Probable | Possible |\n|----------|-------|-----------|----------|----------|\n| CRITICAL | X     | X         | X        | X        |\n| HIGH     | X     | X         | X        | X        |\n| MEDIUM   | X     | X         | X        | X        |\n| LOW      | X     | X         | X        | X        |\n\n### Dependencies\nTotal findings: X (Active: X, Dead: X)\n\n| Package | Version | CVE | Severity | Called? |\n|---------|---------|-----|----------|---------|\n\n### All findings\n\n| File/Package | Finding | CWE | Reachability | Impact | Likelihood | Severity | Confidence |\n|--------------|---------|-----|--------------|--------|------------|----------|------------|","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":211,"totalLines":211,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/commands/security-review-ref.md","time":{"start":1788164258565,"end":1788164258572}},"id":"prt_056e53aff001De9u7rRfxJKNwN","sessionID":"ses_fa923204fffeJOVYIIzNA2JDJK","messageID":"msg_056e5016b001vV8keRv5AD5lFd"}}
