{"type":"text","timestamp":1788165507304,"sessionID":"ses_fa923204fffeJOVYIIzNA2JDJK","part":{"id":"prt_056f80bad001OUsQgqAmpcHDur","messageID":"msg_056f6640c001Qvyonn94h3HAg6","sessionID":"ses_fa923204fffeJOVYIIzNA2JDJK","type":"text","text":"\n\nAll source files reviewed. Two additional findings surface, plus the `base_model.py:11` confirms **predictable sequential integer IDs** (strengthens the IDOR enumeration). Writing a consolidated **CSRF** finding (no token on any state-changing POST) and an `echo=True` **SQL logging** finding, then bumping the delete-IDOR likelihood.\n\n","time":{"start":1788165491629,"end":1788165507302}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788165507309,"sessionID":"ses_fa923204fffeJOVYIIzNA2JDJK","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_4dd0118b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","oldString":"## Pre-processing artifacts","newString":"### All state-changing POST routes — CSRF (no token / SameSite hardening)\n**CWE:** CWE-352\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** MODERATE\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact MODERATE x Likelihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nTransform: State-changing POST endpoints — `/account` (account.py:73), `/account/image` (account.py:93), `/notes` (notes.py:17), `/notes/<id>/delete` (notes.py:39), `/signup` (signup.py:33), `/registration-codes` (registration_codes.py:26) — none implement a CSRF token / `CSRFProtect` / `SameSite` cookie hardening.\nSink: Cross-origin forged request from an attacker-controlled page -> server processes the victim's authenticated session.\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker serves a page that auto-POSTs to `/account` with `is_admin=true` (mass-assignment) or `/account/image` with `url=file:///...` (SSRF) -> 2. Browser sends the victim's authenticated session cookies -> 3. Victim's account is escalated to admin / SSRF triggered without consent (also forces note deletion, password change).\n\n**Mitigations:** None (no CSRF token; session cookies lack `SameSite` hardening).\n**Fix:** Apply `flask_wtf.csrf.csrfProtect`; set `SameSite=Lax/Strict` session cookies; verify origin/`Referer` on state-changing POSTs; require anti-CSRF tokens in forms.\n\n### models/__init__.py:14 — SQL `echo=True` logs sensitive queries to server logs\n**CWE:** CWE-200\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** LOW\n**Likelihood:** LOW\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood LOW = LOW (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `models/__init__.py:14` — `create_engine('sqlite:///' + ..., echo=True)`\nTransform:  `echo=True` logs every executed SQL statement **including bound parameters** to console/server logs\nSink:       server logs (uwsgi stdout) — contain user emails and bcrypt password hashes\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker obtains server logs (log files, uwsgi stdout, centralized logging) -> 2. Reads logged SQL with bound params -> 3. Exposes user emails and bcrypt password hashes.\n\n**Mitigations:** None (`echo` left enabled).\n**Fix:** Set `echo=False` in production; never log query parameters containing credentials.\n\n## Pre-processing artifacts"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n+++ /Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md\n@@ -389,8 +389,43 @@\n **Exploit:** 1. Authenticated user POSTs `/account` with `is_admin=true` (and/or `password=<hash>`) -> 2. `form.data` includes `is_admin` -> 3. `current_user.__dict__.update` sets `is_admin=True`, `session.commit()` promotes the account to admin (privilege escalation).\n **Mitigations:** `email` change is guarded (line 78); `is_admin`/`password` are not (unchecked mass-assignment).\n **Fix:** Do not map form data onto ORM objects wholesale. Assign only whitelisted fields (`email`/`password` via `hashpw`); never copy `is_admin` or other privileged columns from form input.\n \n+### All state-changing POST routes — CSRF (no token / SameSite hardening)\n+**CWE:** CWE-352\n+**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n+**Impact:** MODERATE\n+**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n+**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n+**Severity:** Impact MODERATE x Likelihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (