{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788165758969,"sessionID":"ses_fa923204fffeJOVYIIzNA2JDJK","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_c6844957","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Security Assessment — 2026-08-31 — Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit\n2: \n3: ## Context\n4: **Project:** Extremely Vulnerable Flask App — intentionally vulnerable educational web app\n5: **Language/framework:** Python 3.13 / Flask; SQLAlchemy + SQLite; Jinja2 templating; Bootstrap-Flask\n6: **Purpose:** Educational demonstration of common web vulnerabilities. Registration is invite-based; ships with predefined `user@evfa.com:user` and `admin@evfa.com:admin` accounts and a leaked invite code in the README.\n7: **Deployment:** Docker container — nginx (`conf/nginx.conf`) proxying to uwsgi (`uwsgi.ini`, `module = app:app`) over `/tmp/uwsgi.socket`. CMD: `service nginx start; uwsgi --ini uwsgi.ini` (5 processes, master).\n8: **Ports/services:** HTTP `:5000:80` (nginx↔uwsgi socket); SQLite `database.db`\n9: **Auth model:** Invite-based registration with admin/user roles (to be confirmed in route analysis — no OAuth/JWT visible)\n10: **Data stores:** SQLite via SQLAlchemy (`database.db`, resettable)\n11: **External integrations:** none visible\n12: **Notes:** Intentionally vulnerable (educational). Leaked invite code published in README. Debug mode and exact auth mechanism to be confirmed from `app.py`/routes in step 6.\n13: \n14: ## graphify-out\n15: graphify-out not available — `graph.json` present but `GRAPH_REPORT.md` was not generated (both required for graphify-based analysis). Step 4b (attack-path / dead-code via graphify) skipped; attack surface assessed via manual grep.\n16: \n17: ## Semgrep baseline\n18: 19 files scanned (23 discovered, 4 `__init__.py` excluded by scanner). Findings (ERROR/WARNING only; test/generated/non-source excluded):\n19: \n20: | file:line | rule-name | severity | CWE |\n21: |---|---|---|---|\n22: | routes/account.py:33 | avoid-sqlalchemy-text | ERROR | CWE-89 SQLi (sqlalchemy.text) |\n23: | routes/account.py:105 | secure-set-cookie | WARNING | CWE-614 insecure cookie |\n24: | routes/account.py:105 | insecure-deserialization | ERROR | CWE-502 pickle |\n25: | routes/account.py:105 | avoid-pickle | WARNING | CWE-502 pickle |\n26: | routes/account.py:118 | avoid-pickle | WARNING | CWE-502 pickle |\n27: | routes/account.py:128 | avoid-pickle | WARNING | CWE-502 pickle |\n28: | app.py:31 | render-template-string | WARNING | CWE-96 SSTI (render_template_string) |\n29: | utils/profile_image.py:7 | dynamic-urllib-use-detected | WARNING | CWE-939 urllib file:// |\n30: \n31: Notes: all findings fingerprinted `requires login`; Semgrep flagged only `account.py`, `app.py`, `utils/profile_image.py`. Manual review required for business-logic / access-control / IDOR / SSRF that patterns miss.\n32: \n33: **Serena symbol overviews (retained for step 6):**\n34: - `app.py`: Variables `app, bootstrap, login_manager, ckeditor`; Functions `unauthorized, page_not_found`.\n35: - `routes/login.py`: Functions `load_user, login, do_login, logout, logged_in`.\n36: - `routes/account.py`: Functions `account, search, get_personal_notes, add_image, update_account, toggle_darkmode, before_request, after_request`; Variable `default_preferences`.\n37: \n38: ## Secret scan baseline\n39: LeakFerret (`scan_repository`) — not available; tool not in toolset. Skipped. Manual secret check deferred to step 6 (grep for hardcoded secrets/tokens).\n40: \n41: ## Dependency scan baseline\n42: | package | version | CVE | severity | fixed-in |\n43: |---|---|---|---|---|\n44: | werkzeug | (required by requirements.txt) | CVE-2026-27199 (GHSA-29vq-49wr-vm6x) | Medium | 3.1.6 |\n45: \n46: Note: CWE-67 path traversal — `safe_join`/`send_from_directory` allows Windows special device names (e.g. `example/NUL`) only when the app runs on Windows. App runs in Docker/Linux, so exploitability is likely limited; verify whether `send_from_directory`/`safe_join` is used with user-controlled paths in step 6.\n47: \n48: ## Attack surface\n49: Sources mapped via grep (31 route decorators, 6 user-input sites, 2 SQL-interpolation sites, 1 urlopen, 1 render_template_string, 3 pickle sites, 1 hardcoded secret_key, 0 CSRF protections).\n50: \n51: ### Entry points\n52: | # | Type | Location | Auth required | Description |\n53: |---|------|----------|---------------|-------------|\n54: | 1 | HTTP route `/` | routes/home.py:8 | No (public) | Landing page |\n55: | 2 | HTTP route `/home` | routes/home.py:14 | Yes | Home feed |\n56: | 3 | HTTP route `/signup` GET+POST | routes/signup.py:28,33 | No (public) | Invite-registration; raw SQL code lookup (signup.py:17) |\n57: | 4 | HTTP route `/login` GET+POST | routes/login.py:17,22 | No (public) | Authentication |\n58: | 5 | HTTP route `/logout` | routes/login.py:43 | Yes | Session end |\n59: | 6 | HTTP route `/is_logged_in` | routes/login.py:50 | No (public) | Auth state check (info disclosure) |\n60: | 7 | HTTP route `/account` GET | routes/account.py:18 | Yes | Account dashboard |\n61: | 8 | HTTP route `/search` GET | routes/account.py:24 | Yes | `request.args['search']` → SQLAlchemy text() (account.py:33) |\n62: | 9 | HTTP route `/account/image` POST | routes/account.py:51 | Yes | Image upload → `urlopen(url)` (profile_image.py:7) |\n63: | 10 | HTTP route `/account` POST | routes/account.py:68 | Yes | Profile/password update |\n64: | 11 | HTTP route `/darkmode` POST | routes/account.py:98 | Yes | Preference toggle |\n65: | 12 | HTTP route `/accounts/<int:user_id>/notes` | routes/account.py:41 | Yes | Other user's notes (IDOR surface) |\n66: | 13 | HTTP route `/notes` GET+POST | routes/notes.py:10,16 | Yes | List/create notes |\n67: | 14 | HTTP route `/notes/<int:note_id>/delete` POST | routes/notes.py:39 | Yes | Delete by id (IDOR surface) |\n68: | 15 | HTTP route `/registration-codes` GET+POST | routes/registration_codes.py:12,26 | Yes | Admin code management |\n69: \n70: ### Trust boundaries\n71: | # | Boundary | Location | Data type |\n72: |---|----------|----------|-----------|\n73: | 1 | User `search` param → SQLAlchemy `text()` SQL | routes/account.py:27→33 | SQL string (CWE-89) |\n74: | 2 | User registration code → raw SQL string interpolation | routes/signup.py:35→17 | SQL string (CWE-89) |\n75: | 3 | Pickled data → `pickle.loads` | routes/account.py:105,118,128 | Untrusted object (CWE-502) |\n76: | 4 | User-provided image URL → `urlopen()` | utils/profile_image.py:7 | URL (CWE-939/20 SSRF/file) |\n77: | 5 | User input → `render_template_string` | app.py:31 | Template (CWE-96 SSTI) |\n78: | 6 | Session/cookie → Flask-Login `login_manager` + `logged_in()` | routes/login.py | Auth (CWE-30) |\n79: | 7 | IDOR: `<int:user_id>`, `<int:note_id>` with no ownership check | routes/account.py:41, routes/notes.py:39 | Authorization (CWE-639) |\n80: | 8 | Hardcoded `app.secret_key` | app.py:11 | Secret (CWE-798) |\n81: \n82: ### Notes\n83: - No CSRF protection detected (0 matches for `csrf`/`flask_wtf`/`generate_csrf`) despite state-changing POST forms — potential CSRF (CWE-352) to verify in step 6.\n84: - Public, unauthenticated entry points: `/`, `/signup`, `/login`, `/is_logged_in`.\n85: - Registration uses `uuid4()` codes (registration_codes.py:34) but `db_seed.py:9` ships a hardcoded, README-published invite code (`a36e990b-...`).\n86: - Passwords hashed with `hashpw`/`gensalt` (bcrypt); `app.secret_key` hardcoded as `\"super secret key\"`.\n87: - `db_seed.py` seeds predefined `user@evfa.com:user` and `admin@evfa.com:admin` accounts.\n88: \n89: ## Scanned files\n90: 23 source files (`*.py`, excluding tests/migrations/vendor/.venv/dist/build/.security-output/graphify-out):\n91: \n92: - `app.py` (entry point / Flask factory)\n93: - `db_seed.py` (DB seeding)\n94: - `routes/account.py` (search, image upload, profile — highest risk)\n95: - `routes/login.py` (auth, Flask-Login)\n96: - `routes/notes.py` (notes CRUD, delete-by-id)\n97: - `routes/home.py` (home feed)\n98: - `routes/signup.py` (invite registration, raw SQL)\n99: - `routes/registration_codes.py` (admin code mgmt)\n100: - `routes/__init__.py`\n101: - `models/user.py`, `models/note.py`, `models/registration_code.py`, `models/base_model.py`, `models/__init__.py`\n102: - `forms/account_form.py`, `forms/login_form.py`, `forms/registration_form.py`, `forms/note_form.py`, `forms/image_form.py`, `forms/__init__.py`\n103: - `utils/profile_image.py` (urlopen), `utils/notes.py`, `utils/__init__.py`\n104: \n105: ## Findings\n106: \n107: ### app.py:11 — Hardcoded Flask session secret_key\n108: **CWE:** CWE-259\n109: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n110: **Impact:** CRITICAL\n111: **Likelihood:** HIGH\n112: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n113: **Severity:** Impact CRITICAL x Likelihood HIGH = CRITICAL (ACTIVE)\n114: \n115: **Data flow:**\n116: Source:     `app.py:11` — `app.secret_key` assigned a literal string at app factory\n117: Transform:  `app.py:11` — Flask uses secret_key to sign all session cookies\n118: Sink:       `app.py:11` — attacker who knows the key forges arbitrary session cookies (incl. admin)\n119: \n120: ```python\n121: app.secret_key = \"super secret key\"\n122: ```\n123: \n124: **Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the hardcoded key from the public repo source -> 2. Forges a signed session cookie for `admin@evfa.com` using Flask's `secure_cookies`/`signer` -> 3. Authenticates as admin (full auth bypass).\n125: **Mitigations:** None.\n126: **Fix:** Generate a random secret at runtime (`os.urandom(64)`) or from an environment variable / secrets manager; never hardcode.\n127: \n128: ### app.py:31-33 — Server-Side Template Injection / RCE in 404 handler\n129: **CWE:** CWE-94\n130: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n131: **Impact:** CRITICAL\n132: **Likelihood:** HIGH\n133: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n134: **Severity:** Impact CRITICAL x Likelihood HIGH = CRITICAL (ACTIVE)\n135: \n136: **Data flow:**\n137: Source:     `request.path` — attacker-controlled URL path (any unmatched URL triggers 404)\n138: Transform:  `app.py:32` — f-string interpolates `request.path` into a Jinja2 template literal\n139: Sink:       `app.py:31-33` — `render_template_string(...)` renders the attacker-controlled template (no sandbox) -> Jinja2 RCE\n140: \n141: ```python\n142:     detailed_message = render_template_string(\n143:         f\"{error}. Requested URL was {request.path}\"\n144:     )\n145:     return render_template(\"404.html\", detailed_message=detailed_message)\n146: ```\n147: \n148: **Exploit:** 1. Attacker requests `/{{payload}}` (any unmatched route) -> 2. 404 handler interpolates the URL into `render_template_string` -> 3. Jinja2 evaluates `{{ ''.__class__.__mro__[1].__subclasses__() }}` chain -> RCE.\n149: **Mitigations:** None (no Jinja2 sandbox; `render_template_string` renders full template syntax).\n150: **Fix:** Never pass user input into `render_template_string`. Use `render_template(\"404.html\", path=request.path)` and let Jinja2 escape output, or sanitize/avoid dynamic template construction.\n151: \n152: ### routes/account.py:31-33 — SQL injection via `sqlalchemy.text()`\n153: **CWE:** CWE-89\n154: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n155: **Impact:** HIGH\n156: **Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n157: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n158: **Severity:** Impact HIGH x Likelihood MEDIUM = HIGH (ACTIVE)\n159: \n160: **Data flow:**\n161: Source:     `routes/account.py:27` — `request.args.get('search', '')` (user-controlled)\n162: Transform:  `routes/account.py:33` — f-string injects `search_param` into `text(\"text like '%...%'\")`\n163: Sink:       `routes/account.py:33` — `text(...)` passes constructed SQL to the DB unchanged (bypasses parameterization)\n164: \n165: ```python\n166: personal_notes = session.query(Note).filter(\n167:     Note.user_id == current_user.id,\n168:     text(f\"text like '%{search_param}%'')).all()\n169: ```\n170: \n171: **Exploit:** 1. Authenticated user requests `/search?search=' UNION SELECT id,email,password FROM users--` -> 2. Parameter is concatenated into raw SQL via `text()` -> 3. UNION-based exfiltration of other users' data / bypass of the `user_id` filter.\n172: **Mitigations:** None (raw `text()` bypasses SQLAlchemy parameterization; the `user_id` filter is ANDed but can be escaped via injection).\n173: **Fix:** Parameterize: `text(\"text like :q\").bindparams(text('q', search_param + \"%\"))` or use `Note.text.like(...)` with bound params; never f-string raw SQL.\n174: \n175: ### routes/account.py:118 — Insecure deserialization / RCE via `pickle.loads` on cookie\n176: **CWE:** CWE-502\n177: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n178: **Impact:** CRITICAL\n179: **Likelihood:** HIGH\n180: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n181: **Severity:** Impact CRITICAL x Likelihood HIGH = CRITICAL (ACTIVE)\n182: \n183: **Data flow:**\n184: Source:     `routes/account.py:114` — attacker-controlled `preferences` cookie (`request.cookies.get('preferences')`)\n185: Transform:  `routes/account.py:118` — `b64decode(preferences)` decodes base64 payload\n186: Sink:       `routes/account.py:118` — `loads(...)` = `pickle.loads` -> arbitrary object construction -> RCE. Triggered by `@app.before_request`, which runs on every request including public routes (e.g. `/login`).\n187: \n188: ```python\n189: preferences = request.cookies.get('preferences')\n190: if preferences is None:\n191:     preferences = default_preferences\n192: else:\n193:     preferences = loads(b64decode(preferences))\n194: ```\n195: \n196: **Exploit:** 1. Attacker crafts a base64(pickle) payload that executes code on `pickle.loads` -> 2. Sends it as the `preferences` cookie to any route (before_request runs before auth) -> 3. `pickle.loads` deserializes -> RCE.\n197: **Mitigations:** None. Cookie also written unpickled at line 105 without `secure`/`httponly`/`samesite` (CWE-614), but the deserialization is the critical issue.\n198: **Fix:** Remove `pickle` entirely; store preferences as JSON (`json.dumps`/`json.loads`) or signed tokens. Never `pickle.loads` untrusted input.\n199: \n200: ### routes/account.py:43-46 — Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) on other users' notes\n201: **CWE:** CWE-284\n202: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n203: **Impact:** MODERATE\n204: **Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n205: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n206: **Severity:** Impact MODERATE x Likelihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (ACTIVE)\n207: \n208: **Data flow:**\n209: Source:     `routes/account.py:41` — `<int:user_id>` from URL path\n210: Transform:  `routes/account.py:45-46` — `session.query(Note).filter(Note.user_id == user_id)` — no check that `user_id == current_user.id`\n211: Sink:       `routes/account.py:47` — other user's notes returned to the requester\n212: \n213: ```python\n214: def get_personal_notes(user_id: int):\n215:     with Session() as session:\n216:         personal_notes = session.query(Note).filter(\n217:             Note.user_id == user_id).all()\n218: ```\n219: \n220: **Exploit:** 1. Authenticated user visits `/accounts/<any-user-id>/notes` -> 2. Query returns that user's notes (name collision lets attacker enumerate IDs) -> 3. Cross-user data exposure.\n221: **Mitigations:** None (route enforces authentication but not authorization/ownership).\n222: **Fix:** Enforce `user_id == current_user.id` (403/404 otherwise); scope queries to `current_user`.\n223: \n224: ### routes/signup.py:15-18 — SQL injection on public `/signup` (password-hash exfiltration)\n225: **CWE:** CWE-89\n226: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n227: **Impact:** HIGH\n228: **Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n229: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n230: **Severity:** Impact HIGH x Likelihood MEDIUM = HIGH (ACTIVE)\n231: \n232: **Data flow:**\n233: Source:     `routes/signup.py:45` — `form.registration_code.data` (user-controlled, public `/signup` POST)\n234: Transform:  `routes/signup.py:46` — `validate_token(code, session)` interpolates `code` into `text(f\"...WHERE code = '{code}'\")`\n235: Sink:       `routes/signup.py:15-18` — `session.execute(text(...))` runs raw SQL; `result.id` returns the first column, which a UNION payload can make a user's bcrypt hash\n236: \n237: ```python\n238: result = session.execute(\n239:     text(f\"\"\"\n240:         SELECT id, code FROM {RegistrationCode.__tablename__} WHERE code = '{code}'\n241:     \"\"\")).first()\n242: ```\n243: \n244: **Exploit:** 1. Attacker POSTs `/signup` with `registration_code` = `' AND 1=0 UNION SELECT password, id FROM users LIMIT 1--` -> 2. Base query returns nothing, UNION returns `(bcrypt_hash, user_id)`; `result.id` = the hash -> 3. Collect hashes one request at a time, offline-crack bcrypt. (The line-52 `token.code != code` double-check blocks auth-bypass but not UNION exfiltration.)\n245: **Mitigations:** Partial — line 52 double-check blocks registration-bypass; `except OperationalError` suppresses error-based leakage. UNION exfiltration of the first column still works.\n246: **Fix:** Parameterize: `text(\"SELECT id, code FROM registration_codes WHERE code = :c\").bindparams(text('c', code))`. Never interpolate user input into `text()`.\n247: \n248: ### routes/login.py:50-56 — Auth status / email disclosure on public `/is_logged_in`\n249: **CWE:** CWE-200\n250: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n251: **Impact:** LOW\n252: **Likelihood:** HIGH\n253: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n254: **Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood HIGH = LOW (ACTIVE)\n255: \n256: **Data flow:**\n257: Source:     `routes/login.py:52-55` — response body built from `current_user.is_authenticated` and `current_user.email`\n258: Transform:  `routes/login.py:50` — `/is_logged_in` has no `@login_required` (public)\n259: Sink:       `routes/login.py:52-55` — JSON response returns authenticated user's email + auth flag\n260: \n261: ```python\n262: @app.route('/is_logged_in', methods=['GET'])\n263: def logged_in():\n264:     return {\n265:         'is_logged_in': current_user.is_authenticated,\n266:         'username':\n267:         current_user.email if current_user.is_authenticated else '-'\n268:     }\n269: ```\n270: \n271: **Exploit:** 1. Attacker (or a logged-in victim's context) GETs `/is_logged_in` -> 2. Response echoes the authenticated user's email address and auth status -> 3. Confirms an email is a registered/authenticated account (account enumeration aid).\n272: **Mitigations:** None (endpoint is public; returns email only for authenticated sessions).\n273: **Fix:** Enforce `@login_required`; return a generic boolean without the email, or remove the endpoint.\n274: \n275: ### utils/profile_image.py:7 — SSRF / arbitrary file read via `urlopen(url)`\n276: **CWE:** CWE-918\n277: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n278: **Impact:** HIGH\n279: **Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n280: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n281: **Severity:** Impact HIGH x Likelihood MEDIUM = HIGH (ACTIVE)\n282: \n283: **Data flow:**\n284: Source:     `routes/account.py:60` — `get_base64_image_blob(form.url.data)` (user-provided URL via `/account/image` POST)\n285: Transform:  `utils/profile_image.py:11-12` — `get_base64_image_blob(url)` -> `download(url)`\n286: Sink:       `utils/profile_image.py:7` — `urlopen(url)` with no scheme validation -> `file://` reads local files; `http://169.254.169.254/` SSRF to cloud metadata/internal services\n287: \n288: ```python\n289: def download(url: str) -> bytes:\n290:     with urlopen(url) as response:\n291:         return response.read()\n292: ```\n293: \n294: **Exploit:** 1. Authenticated user POSTs `/account/image` with `url=file:///etc/passwd` (or `http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/`) -> 2. `urlopen` fetches it (scheme unvalidated; `guess_type` only sets mimetype) -> 3. Base64 blob returned/stored -> arbitrary local file read or SSRF to internal endpoints.\n295: **Mitigations:** None (no URL scheme allowlist; only `guess_type` for mimetype).\n296: **Fix:** Allowlist URL schemes (`https` only); block `file://`, `gopher:`, internal IPs; fetch server-side with a bounded whitelist; never pass user-controlled URLs to `urlopen`.\n297: \n298: ### routes/notes.py:41-48 — IDOR: delete any user's note by `note_id`\n299: **CWE:** CWE-284\n300: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n301: **Impact:** MODERATE\n302: **Likelihood:** HIGH (note IDs are sequential auto-increment integers — `models/base_model.py:11`; `/notes/<id>/delete` is trivially enumerable)\n303: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n304: **Severity:** Impact MODERATE x Likelihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (ACTIVE)\n305: \n306: **Data flow:**\n307: Source:     `routes/notes.py:39` — `<int:note_id>` from URL path\n308: Transform:  `routes/notes.py:44` — `session.get(Note, note_id)` — no `note.user_id == current_user.id` check\n309: Sink:       `routes/notes.py:48` — `session.delete(note)` deletes another user's note\n310: \n311: ```python\n312: def delete_note(note_id: int):\n313:     with Session() as session:\n314:         note = session.get(Note, note_id)\n315:         if note is None:\n316:             flash('Note not found', 'warning')\n317:         else:\n318:             session.delete(note)\n319:             session.commit()\n320: ```\n321: \n322: **Exploit:** 1. Authenticated user POSTs `/notes/<any-note-id>/delete` -> 2. Server loads and deletes the note regardless of owner -> 3. Destruction of other users' notes (data tampering).\n323: **Mitigations:** None (enforces authentication, not ownership).\n324: **Fix:** Check `note.user_id == current_user.id` before deleting (404 otherwise); scope to `current_user`.\n325: \n326: ### db_seed.py:9 — Hardcoded, README-published registration code\n327: **CWE:** CWE-259\n328: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n329: **Impact:** LOW\n330: **Likelihood:** HIGH\n331: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n332: **Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood HIGH = LOW (ACTIVE)\n333: \n334: **Data flow:**\n335: Source:     `db_seed.py:9` — static registration code literal `'a36e990b-0024-4d55-b74a-f8d7528e1764'`\n336: Transform:  `db_seed.py:10` — seeded into `RegistrationCode` table at startup (`setup_db()`, called from `app.py:21` on fresh DB)\n337: Sink:       `db_seed.py:9` — published verbatim in `README.md` (\"use the leaked invite code ...\")\n338: \n339: ```python\n340: if session.query(RegistrationCode).count() == 0:\n341:     static_code = 'a36e990b-0024-4d55-b74a-f8d7528e1764'\n342:     session.add(RegistrationCode(static_code))\n343: ```\n344: \n345: **Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the code from the public README -> 2. Uses it on `/signup` to create an account -> 3. Unauthorized account creation (bypasses invite generation).\n346: **Mitigations:** None (code is hardcoded and publicly documented).\n347: **Fix:** Generate registration codes at runtime; never hardcode or publish invite codes.\n348: \n349: ### db_seed.py:18-19 — Admin account with weak, known password (`'admin'`)\n350: **CWE:** CWE-259\n351: **Reachability:** CONDITIONAL\n352: **Impact:** HIGH\n353: **Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n354: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n355: **Severity:** Impact HIGH x Likelihood MEDIUM = HIGH (CONDITIONAL)\n356: \n357: **Data flow:**\n358: Source:     `db_seed.py:18-19` — admin account seeded with `hashpw(b'admin', gensalt())` (password is literally `'admin'`)\n359: Transform:  `db_seed.py:22` — admin (`is_admin=True`) created on fresh DB (`User.count() == 0`)\n360: Sink:       login (`routes/login.py:32`) — `bcrypt.checkpw` verifies against the cracked hash\n361: \n362: ```python\n363: admin = User('admin@evfa.com',\n364:              hashpw(b'admin', gensalt()).decode(), True)\n365: ```\n366: \n367: **Exploit:** 1. On a freshly-seeded DB, admin's bcrypt hash corresponds to the password `'admin'` -> 2. Attacker obtains the hash (e.g., via the `/signup` SQLi exfiltration) -> 3. `'admin'` cracks in seconds; logs in as admin (privilege escalation).\n368: **Mitigations:** Password is bcrypt-hashed (not plaintext), but `'admin'` is a top-common password, cracked instantly offline.\n369: **Fix:** Do not ship predefined admin accounts with weak passwords; force password change on first login; use strong randomly-generated seeds.\n370: \n371: ### forms/account_form.py:4 + routes/account.py:81 — Mass-assignment → privilege escalation (`is_admin`)\n372: **CWE:** CWE-284\n373: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n374: **Impact:** HIGH\n375: **Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n376: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n377: **Severity:** Impact HIGH x Likelihood MEDIUM = HIGH (ACTIVE)\n378: \n379: **Data flow:**\n380: Source:     `forms/account_form.py:4` — `is_admin = BooleanField('Is Admin')` (field present in submitted form)\n381: Transform:  `routes/account.py:81` — `current_user.__dict__.update(form.data)` copies ALL form fields onto the user object\n382: Sink:       `routes/account.py:84` — `session.commit()` persists `is_admin` (and `password`/`email`) to the DB\n383: \n384: ```python\n385: current_user.__dict__.update(form.data)\n386: session.commit()\n387: ```\n388: \n389: **Exploit:** 1. Authenticated user POSTs `/account` with `is_admin=true` (and/or `password=<hash>`) -> 2. `form.data` includes `is_admin` -> 3. `current_user.__dict__.update` sets `is_admin=True`, `session.commit()` promotes the account to admin (privilege escalation).\n390: **Mitigations:** `email` change is guarded (line 78); `is_admin`/`password` are not (unchecked mass-assignment).\n391: **Fix:** Do not map form data onto ORM objects wholesale. Assign only whitelisted fields (`email`/`password` via `hashpw`); never copy `is_admin` or other privileged columns from form input.\n392: \n393: ### All state-changing POST routes — CSRF (no token / SameSite hardening)\n394: **CWE:** CWE-352\n395: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n396: **Impact:** MODERATE\n397: **Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n398: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n399: **Severity:** Impact MODERATE x Likelihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (ACTIVE)\n400: \n401: **Data flow:**\n402: Transform: State-changing POST endpoints — `/account` (account.py:73), `/account/image` (account.py:93), `/notes` (notes.py:17), `/notes/<id>/delete` (notes.py:39), `/signup` (signup.py:33), `/registration-codes` (registration_codes.py:26) — none implement a CSRF token / `CSRFProtect` / `SameSite` cookie hardening.\n403: Sink: Cross-origin forged request from an attacker-controlled page -> server processes the victim's authenticated session.\n404: \n405: **Exploit:** 1. Attacker serves a page that auto-POSTs to `/account` with `is_admin=true` (mass-assignment) or `/account/image` with `url=file:///...` (SSRF) -> 2. Browser sends the victim's authenticated session cookies -> 3. Victim's account is escalated to admin / SSRF triggered without consent (also forces note deletion, password change).\n406: \n407: **Mitigations:** None (no CSRF token; session cookies lack `SameSite` hardening).\n408: **Fix:** Apply `flask_wtf.csrf.csrfProtect`; set `SameSite=Lax/Strict` session cookies; verify origin/`Referer` on state-changing POSTs; require anti-CSRF tokens in forms.\n409: \n410: ### models/__init__.py:14 — SQL `echo=True` logs sensitive queries to server logs\n411: **CWE:** CWE-200\n412: **Reachability:** ACTIVE\n413: **Impact:** LOW\n414: **Likelihood:** LOW\n415: **Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n416: **Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood LOW = LOW (ACTIVE)\n417: \n418: **Data flow:**\n419: Source:     `models/__init__.py:14` — `create_engine('sqlite:///' + ..., echo=True)`\n420: Transform:  `echo=True` logs every executed SQL statement **including bound parameters** to console/server logs\n421: Sink:       server logs (uwsgi stdout) — contain user emails and bcrypt password hashes\n422: \n423: **Exploit:** 1. Attacker obtains server logs (log files, uwsgi stdout, centralized logging) -> 2. Reads logged SQL with bound params -> 3. Exposes user emails and bcrypt password hashes.\n424: \n425: **Mitigations:** None (`echo` left enabled).\n426: **Fix:** Set `echo=False` in production; never log query parameters containing credentials.\n427: \n428: ## Dependency scan\n429: No `DIFF_SCOPE.md` present — scanned the whole project (no diff-scoping). Grype baseline + OSV-Scanner (PyPI, `requirements.txt`).\n430: \n431: **Grype baseline** (pre-processing):\n432: - `werkzeug@3.1.5` → CVE-2026-27199 (GHSA-29vq-49wr-vm6x), Medium, CWE-67, fixed in 3.1.6.\n433: \n434: **OSV-Scanner** (whole-project):\n435: | Package | Version | CVE / PYSEC | Severity (CVSS) | Fix |\n436: |---|---|---|---|---|\n437: | click | 8.1.7 | PYSEC-2026-2132 (CVE-2026-7246) — command injection in `click.edit()` | High (7.2) | 8.3.3 |\n438: | flask | 3.1.1 | PYSEC-2026-2151 | Medium (4.3) | 3.1.3 |\n439: | werkzeug | 3.1.5 | PYSEC-2026-2320 | Medium (6.3) | 3.1.6 |\n440: \n441: **Diff (baseline → OSV-Scanner):** `click` (High) and `flask` (Medium) are new vs the grype baseline; `werkzeug` carries a second, distinct CVE (OSV: PYSEC-2026-2320 vs grype: CVE-2026-27199). All three are upstream dependencies (Flask → click; Flask/Werkzeug).\n442: **Note:** `click` command injection is confined to `click.edit()` (interactive editor), which this app does not call — so actual exploitability is low despite the High CVSS. `flask`/`werkzeug` vulns are library-level (patch to update).\n443: **Fix:** Pin `click>=8.3.3`, `flask>=3.1.3`, `werkzeug>=3.1.6`; re-audit.\n444: \n445: ## Summary tables\n446: \n447: ### Table 1 — All findings by severity\n448: | # | Location | CWE | Reachability | Severity |\n449: |---|---|---|---|---|\n450: | 1 | app.py:11 | CWE-259 (hardcoded secret) | ACTIVE | CRITICAL |\n451: | 2 | app.py:31-33 | CWE-94 (SSTI/RCE) | ACTIVE | CRITICAL |\n452: | 3 | account.py:118 | CWE-502 (pickle.loads RCE) | ACTIVE | CRITICAL |\n453: | 4 | account.py:33 | CWE-89 (SQLi) | ACTIVE | HIGH |\n454: | 5 | signup.py:15-18 | CWE-89 (SQLi, public /signup) | ACTIVE | HIGH |\n455: | 6 | profile_image.py:7 | CWE-918 (SSRF/file://) | ACTIVE | HIGH |\n456: | 7 | db_seed.py:18-19 | CWE-259 (weak admin password) | CONDITIONAL | HIGH |\n457: | 8 | account_form.py:4 + account.py:81 | CWE-284 (mass-assignment → admin) | ACTIVE | HIGH |\n458: | 9 | account.py:43-46 | CWE-284 (IDOR read notes) | ACTIVE | MEDIUM |\n459: | 10 | notes.py:41-48 | CWE-284 (IDOR delete notes) | ACTIVE | MEDIUM |\n460: | 11 | routes/* (all POST) | CWE-352 (CSRF) | ACTIVE | MEDIUM |\n461: | 12 | login.py:50-56 | CWE-200 (email/auth disclosure) | ACTIVE | LOW |\n462: | 13 | db_seed.py:9 | CWE-259 (hardcoded invite code) | ACTIVE | LOW |\n463: | 14 | models/__init__.py:14 | CWE-200 (SQL echo logs) | ACTIVE | LOW |\n464: \n465: **Totals:** CRITICAL 3, HIGH 5, MEDIUM 3, LOW 3 (14 findings).\n466: \n467: ### Table 2 — Findings by vulnerability type\n468: | Type | Findings | Count |\n469: |---|---|---|\n470: | SQL Injection (CWE-89) | #4, #5 | 2 |\n471: | Server-Side Template Injection / RCE (CWE-94) | #2 | 1 |\n472: | Insecure Deserialization / RCE (CWE-502) | #3 | 1 |\n473: | SSRF / Arbitrary File Read (CWE-918) | #6 | 1 |\n474: | Broken Access Control — IDOR (CWE-284) | #9, #10 | 2 |\n475: | Broken Access Control — Mass-assignment / Privilege Escalation (CWE-284) | #8 | 1 |\n476: | Cross-Site Request Forgery (CWE-352) | #11 | 1 |\n477: | Hardcoded Credentials / Secrets (CWE-259) | #1, #7, #13 | 3 |\n478: | Information Exposure (CWE-200) | #12, #14 | 2 |\n479: \n480: ### Top risks (active, highest priority)\n481: 1. **`account.py:118` pickle.loads RCE** — unauthenticated (via `before_request`), no auth/session needed → full server compromise. **Fix:** never `pickle.loads`; validate/parse JSON.\n482: 2. **`app.py:31-33` SSTI/RCE** — `render_template_string(request.path)` in the 404 handler → attacker-controlled template → RCE. **Fix:** serve a static 404 page; never `render_template_string` on user input.\n483: 3. **`app.py:11` hardcoded `secret_key`** — session forgery (sign any session, forge admin). **Fix:** read from env/secret manager.\n484: 4. **`account.py:81` mass-assignment → `is_admin`** — authenticated admin escalation (unlocks the admin-only `/registration-codes` gate). **Fix:** whitelist fields; never `__dict__.update(form.data)`.\n485: 5. **`account.py:33` / `signup.py:17` SQLi** — parameterize `text()`; don't interpolate.\n486: \n487: ### Remediation roadmap (prioritized)\n488: **P0 — Fix now (RCE / full compromise):**\n489: - `account.py:118` — replace `pickle.loads(cookie)` with a validated format (e.g., HMAC-signed JSON); run deserialization only on trusted data.\n490: - `app.py:31-33` — return a static 404; remove `render_template_string`.\n491: - `app.py:11` — move `secret_key` to an environment variable / secrets store.\n492: \n493: **P1 — Fix soon (authn/authz / data):**\n494: - `account.py:33` + `signup.py:17` — parameterize all SQL (bind params); never `text(f\"...{var}...\")`.\n495: - `account_form.py:4` + `account.py:81` — assign only whitelisted fields (`email`, bcrypt'd `password`); never copy `is_admin`/`password` from `form.data`.\n496: - `profile_image.py:7` — allowlist URL scheme (https only), block `file://`/internal IPs; fetch server-side.\n497: - `notes.py:41-48` + `account.py:43-46` — enforce `owner == current_user.id` (404/403 otherwise); IDs are sequential (enumerable).\n498: - `db_seed.py:18-19` — remove the seeded admin account with password `'admin'` (crackable); force password reset on first login.\n499: \n500: **P2 — Harden:**\n501: - Add CSRF protection (`CSRFProtect` / `SameSite` cookies) to all state-changing POSTs.\n502: - `db_seed.py:9` — stop hardcoding/publishing invite codes; generate at runtime.\n503: - `models/__init__.py:14` — set `echo=False`; never log query parameters.\n504: - `login.py:50-56` — remove email/auth disclosure from `/is_logged_in` (or gate it).\n505: \n506: **P3 — Supply chain:**\n507: - Upgrade `click>=8.3.3`, `flask>=3.1.3`, `werkzeug>=3.1.6`; re-audit on version changes.\n508: \n509: ## Pre-processing artifacts\n510: - SBOM available: `.security-output/sbom.cyclonedx.json` (used in step 7).\n511: - Grype results present: `.security-output/grype-results.json` (summarized above).\n512: - `DIFF_SCOPE.md`: not present — no diff-scoping; all files reviewed per step 6 priority.\n\n(End of file - total 512 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Security Assessment — 2026-08-31 — Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit\n\n## Context\n**Project:** Extremely Vulnerable Flask App — intentionally vulnerable educational web app\n**Language/framework:** Python 3.13 / Flask; SQLAlchemy + SQLite; Jinja2 templating; Bootstrap-Flask\n**Purpose:** Educational demonstration of common web vulnerabilities. Registration is invite-based; ships with predefined `user@evfa.com:user` and `admin@evfa.com:admin` accounts and a leaked invite code in the README.\n**Deployment:** Docker container — nginx (`conf/nginx.conf`) proxying to uwsgi (`uwsgi.ini`, `module = app:app`) over `/tmp/uwsgi.socket`. CMD: `service nginx start; uwsgi --ini uwsgi.ini` (5 processes, master).\n**Ports/services:** HTTP `:5000:80` (nginx↔uwsgi socket); SQLite `database.db`\n**Auth model:** Invite-based registration with admin/user roles (to be confirmed in route analysis — no OAuth/JWT visible)\n**Data stores:** SQLite via SQLAlchemy (`database.db`, resettable)\n**External integrations:** none visible\n**Notes:** Intentionally vulnerable (educational). Leaked invite code published in README. Debug mode and exact auth mechanism to be confirmed from `app.py`/routes in step 6.\n\n## graphify-out\ngraphify-out not available — `graph.json` present but `GRAPH_REPORT.md` was not generated (both required for graphify-based analysis). Step 4b (attack-path / dead-code via graphify) skipped; attack surface assessed via manual grep.\n\n## Semgrep baseline\n19 files scanned (23 discovered, 4 `__init__.py` excluded by scanner). Findings (ERROR/WARNING only; test/generated/non-source excluded):\n\n| file:line | rule-name | severity | CWE |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/mikey/HomeWorks/OpenCode-tests/test-vuln-flask/.security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","text":"# Security Assessment — 2026-08-31 — Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit\n\n## Context\n**Project:** Extremely Vulnerable Flask App — intentionally vulnerable educational web app\n**Language/framework:** Python 3.13 / Flask; SQLAlchemy + SQLite; Jinja2 templating; Bootstrap-Flask\n**Purpose:** Educational demonstration of common web vulnerabilities. Registration is invite-based; ships with predefined `user@evfa.com:user` and `admin@evfa.com:admin` accounts and a leaked invite code in the README.\n**Deployment:** Docker container — nginx (`conf/nginx.conf`) proxying to uwsgi (`uwsgi.ini`, `module = app:app`) over `/tmp/uwsgi.socket`. CMD: `service nginx start; uwsgi --ini uwsgi.ini` (5 processes, master).\n**Ports/services:** HTTP `:5000:80` (nginx↔uwsgi socket); SQLite `database.db`\n**Auth model:** Invite-based registration with admin/user roles (to be confirmed in route analysis — no OAuth/JWT visible)\n**Data stores:** SQLite via SQLAlchemy (`database.db`, resettable)\n**External integrations:** none visible\n**Notes:** Intentionally vulnerable (educational). Leaked invite code published in README. Debug mode and exact auth mechanism to be confirmed from `app.py`/routes in step 6.\n\n## graphify-out\ngraphify-out not available — `graph.json` present but `GRAPH_REPORT.md` was not generated (both required for graphify-based analysis). Step 4b (attack-path / dead-code via graphify) skipped; attack surface assessed via manual grep.\n\n## Semgrep baseline\n19 files scanned (23 discovered, 4 `__init__.py` excluded by scanner). Findings (ERROR/WARNING only; test/generated/non-source excluded):\n\n| file:line | rule-name | severity | CWE |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| routes/account.py:33 | avoid-sqlalchemy-text | ERROR | CWE-89 SQLi (sqlalchemy.text) |\n| routes/account.py:105 | secure-set-cookie | WARNING | CWE-614 insecure cookie |\n| routes/account.py:105 | insecure-deserialization | ERROR | CWE-502 pickle |\n| routes/account.py:105 | avoid-pickle | WARNING | CWE-502 pickle |\n| routes/account.py:118 | avoid-pickle | WARNING | CWE-502 pickle |\n| routes/account.py:128 | avoid-pickle | WARNING | CWE-502 pickle |\n| app.py:31 | render-template-string | WARNING | CWE-96 SSTI (render_template_string) |\n| utils/profile_image.py:7 | dynamic-urllib-use-detected | WARNING | CWE-939 urllib file:// |\n\nNotes: all findings fingerprinted `requires login`; Semgrep flagged only `account.py`, `app.py`, `utils/profile_image.py`. Manual review required for business-logic / access-control / IDOR / SSRF that patterns miss.\n\n**Serena symbol overviews (retained for step 6):**\n- `app.py`: Variables `app, bootstrap, login_manager, ckeditor`; Functions `unauthorized, page_not_found`.\n- `routes/login.py`: Functions `load_user, login, do_login, logout, logged_in`.\n- `routes/account.py`: Functions `account, search, get_personal_notes, add_image, update_account, toggle_darkmode, before_request, after_request`; Variable `default_preferences`.\n\n## Secret scan baseline\nLeakFerret (`scan_repository`) — not available; tool not in toolset. Skipped. Manual secret check deferred to step 6 (grep for hardcoded secrets/tokens).\n\n## Dependency scan baseline\n| package | version | CVE | severity | fixed-in |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| werkzeug | (required by requirements.txt) | CVE-2026-27199 (GHSA-29vq-49wr-vm6x) | Medium | 3.1.6 |\n\nNote: CWE-67 path traversal — `safe_join`/`send_from_directory` allows Windows special device names (e.g. `example/NUL`) only when the app runs on Windows. App runs in Docker/Linux, so exploitability is likely limited; verify whether `send_from_directory`/`safe_join` is used with user-controlled paths in step 6.\n\n## Attack surface\nSources mapped via grep (31 route decorators, 6 user-input sites, 2 SQL-interpolation sites, 1 urlopen, 1 render_template_string, 3 pickle sites, 1 hardcoded secret_key, 0 CSRF protections).\n\n### Entry points\n| # | Type | Location | Auth required | Description |\n|---|------|----------|---------------|-------------|\n| 1 | HTTP route `/` | routes/home.py:8 | No (public) | Landing page |\n| 2 | HTTP route `/home` | routes/home.py:14 | Yes | Home feed |\n| 3 | HTTP route `/signup` GET+POST | routes/signup.py:28,33 | No (public) | Invite-registration; raw SQL code lookup (signup.py:17) |\n| 4 | HTTP route `/login` GET+POST | routes/login.py:17,22 | No (public) | Authentication |\n| 5 | HTTP route `/logout` | routes/login.py:43 | Yes | Session end |\n| 6 | HTTP route `/is_logged_in` | routes/login.py:50 | No (public) | Auth state check (info disclosure) |\n| 7 | HTTP route `/account` GET | routes/account.py:18 | Yes | Account dashboard |\n| 8 | HTTP route `/search` GET | routes/account.py:24 | Yes | `request.args['search']` → SQLAlchemy text() (account.py:33) |\n| 9 | HTTP route `/account/image` POST | routes/account.py:51 | Yes | Image upload → `urlopen(url)` (profile_image.py:7) |\n| 10 | HTTP route `/account` POST | routes/account.py:68 | Yes | Profile/password update |\n| 11 | HTTP route `/darkmode` POST | routes/account.py:98 | Yes | Preference toggle |\n| 12 | HTTP route `/accounts/<int:user_id>/notes` | routes/account.py:41 | Yes | Other user's notes (IDOR surface) |\n| 13 | HTTP route `/notes` GET+POST | routes/notes.py:10,16 | Yes | List/create notes |\n| 14 | HTTP route `/notes/<int:note_id>/delete` POST | routes/notes.py:39 | Yes | Delete by id (IDOR surface) |\n| 15 | HTTP route `/registration-codes` GET+POST | routes/registration_codes.py:12,26 | Yes | Admin code management |\n\n### Trust boundaries\n| # | Boundary | Location | Data type |\n|---|----------|----------|-----------|\n| 1 | User `search` param → SQLAlchemy `text()` SQL | routes/account.py:27→33 | SQL string (CWE-89) |\n| 2 | User registration code → raw SQL string interpolation | routes/signup.py:35→17 | SQL string (CWE-89) |\n| 3 | Pickled data → `pickle.loads` | routes/account.py:105,118,128 | Untrusted object (CWE-502) |\n| 4 | User-provided image URL → `urlopen()` | utils/profile_image.py:7 | URL (CWE-939/20 SSRF/file) |\n| 5 | User input → `render_template_string` | app.py:31 | Template (CWE-96 SSTI) |\n| 6 | Session/cookie → Flask-Login `login_manager` + `logged_in()` | routes/login.py | Auth (CWE-30) |\n| 7 | IDOR: `<int:user_id>`, `<int:note_id>` with no ownership check | routes/account.py:41, routes/notes.py:39 | Authorization (CWE-639) |\n| 8 | Hardcoded `app.secret_key` | app.py:11 | Secret (CWE-798) |\n\n### Notes\n- No CSRF protection detected (0 matches for `csrf`/`flask_wtf`/`generate_csrf`) despite state-changing POST forms — potential CSRF (CWE-352) to verify in step 6.\n- Public, unauthenticated entry points: `/`, `/signup`, `/login`, `/is_logged_in`.\n- Registration uses `uuid4()` codes (registration_codes.py:34) but `db_seed.py:9` ships a hardcoded, README-published invite code (`a36e990b-...`).\n- Passwords hashed with `hashpw`/`gensalt` (bcrypt); `app.secret_key` hardcoded as `\"super secret key\"`.\n- `db_seed.py` seeds predefined `user@evfa.com:user` and `admin@evfa.com:admin` accounts.\n\n## Scanned files\n23 source files (`*.py`, excluding tests/migrations/vendor/.venv/dist/build/.security-output/graphify-out):\n\n- `app.py` (entry point / Flask factory)\n- `db_seed.py` (DB seeding)\n- `routes/account.py` (search, image upload, profile — highest risk)\n- `routes/login.py` (auth, Flask-Login)\n- `routes/notes.py` (notes CRUD, delete-by-id)\n- `routes/home.py` (home feed)\n- `routes/signup.py` (invite registration, raw SQL)\n- `routes/registration_codes.py` (admin code mgmt)\n- `routes/__init__.py`\n- `models/user.py`, `models/note.py`, `models/registration_code.py`, `models/base_model.py`, `models/__init__.py`\n- `forms/account_form.py`, `forms/login_form.py`, `forms/registration_form.py`, `forms/note_form.py`, `forms/image_form.py`, `forms/__init__.py`\n- `utils/profile_image.py` (urlopen), `utils/notes.py`, `utils/__init__.py`\n\n## Findings\n\n### app.py:11 — Hardcoded Flask session secret_key\n**CWE:** CWE-259\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** CRITICAL\n**Likelihood:** HIGH\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact CRITICAL x Likelihood HIGH = CRITICAL (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `app.py:11` — `app.secret_key` assigned a literal string at app factory\nTransform:  `app.py:11` — Flask uses secret_key to sign all session cookies\nSink:       `app.py:11` — attacker who knows the key forges arbitrary session cookies (incl. admin)\n\n```python\napp.secret_key = \"super secret key\"\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the hardcoded key from the public repo source -> 2. Forges a signed session cookie for `admin@evfa.com` using Flask's `secure_cookies`/`signer` -> 3. Authenticates as admin (full auth bypass).\n**Mitigations:** None.\n**Fix:** Generate a random secret at runtime (`os.urandom(64)`) or from an environment variable / secrets manager; never hardcode.\n\n### app.py:31-33 — Server-Side Template Injection / RCE in 404 handler\n**CWE:** CWE-94\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** CRITICAL\n**Likelihood:** HIGH\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact CRITICAL x Likelihood HIGH = CRITICAL (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `request.path` — attacker-controlled URL path (any unmatched URL triggers 404)\nTransform:  `app.py:32` — f-string interpolates `request.path` into a Jinja2 template literal\nSink:       `app.py:31-33` — `render_template_string(...)` renders the attacker-controlled template (no sandbox) -> Jinja2 RCE\n\n```python\n    detailed_message = render_template_string(\n        f\"{error}. Requested URL was {request.path}\"\n    )\n    return render_template(\"404.html\", detailed_message=detailed_message)\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker requests `/{{payload}}` (any unmatched route) -> 2. 404 handler interpolates the URL into `render_template_string` -> 3. Jinja2 evaluates `{{ ''.__class__.__mro__[1].__subclasses__() }}` chain -> RCE.\n**Mitigations:** None (no Jinja2 sandbox; `render_template_string` renders full template syntax).\n**Fix:** Never pass user input into `render_template_string`. Use `render_template(\"404.html\", path=request.path)` and let Jinja2 escape output, or sanitize/avoid dynamic template construction.\n\n### routes/account.py:31-33 — SQL injection via `sqlalchemy.text()`\n**CWE:** CWE-89\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** HIGH\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact HIGH x Likelihood MEDIUM = HIGH (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `routes/account.py:27` — `request.args.get('search', '')` (user-controlled)\nTransform:  `routes/account.py:33` — f-string injects `search_param` into `text(\"text like '%...%'\")`\nSink:       `routes/account.py:33` — `text(...)` passes constructed SQL to the DB unchanged (bypasses parameterization)\n\n```python\npersonal_notes = session.query(Note).filter(\n    Note.user_id == current_user.id,\n    text(f\"text like '%{search_param}%'')).all()\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Authenticated user requests `/search?search=' UNION SELECT id,email,password FROM users--` -> 2. Parameter is concatenated into raw SQL via `text()` -> 3. UNION-based exfiltration of other users' data / bypass of the `user_id` filter.\n**Mitigations:** None (raw `text()` bypasses SQLAlchemy parameterization; the `user_id` filter is ANDed but can be escaped via injection).\n**Fix:** Parameterize: `text(\"text like :q\").bindparams(text('q', search_param + \"%\"))` or use `Note.text.like(...)` with bound params; never f-string raw SQL.\n\n### routes/account.py:118 — Insecure deserialization / RCE via `pickle.loads` on cookie\n**CWE:** CWE-502\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** CRITICAL\n**Likelihood:** HIGH\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact CRITICAL x Likelihood HIGH = CRITICAL (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `routes/account.py:114` — attacker-controlled `preferences` cookie (`request.cookies.get('preferences')`)\nTransform:  `routes/account.py:118` — `b64decode(preferences)` decodes base64 payload\nSink:       `routes/account.py:118` — `loads(...)` = `pickle.loads` -> arbitrary object construction -> RCE. Triggered by `@app.before_request`, which runs on every request including public routes (e.g. `/login`).\n\n```python\npreferences = request.cookies.get('preferences')\nif preferences is None:\n    preferences = default_preferences\nelse:\n    preferences = loads(b64decode(preferences))\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker crafts a base64(pickle) payload that executes code on `pickle.loads` -> 2. Sends it as the `preferences` cookie to any route (before_request runs before auth) -> 3. `pickle.loads` deserializes -> RCE.\n**Mitigations:** None. Cookie also written unpickled at line 105 without `secure`/`httponly`/`samesite` (CWE-614), but the deserialization is the critical issue.\n**Fix:** Remove `pickle` entirely; store preferences as JSON (`json.dumps`/`json.loads`) or signed tokens. Never `pickle.loads` untrusted input.\n\n### routes/account.py:43-46 — Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) on other users' notes\n**CWE:** CWE-284\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** MODERATE\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact MODERATE x Likelihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `routes/account.py:41` — `<int:user_id>` from URL path\nTransform:  `routes/account.py:45-46` — `session.query(Note).filter(Note.user_id == user_id)` — no check that `user_id == current_user.id`\nSink:       `routes/account.py:47` — other user's notes returned to the requester\n\n```python\ndef get_personal_notes(user_id: int):\n    with Session() as session:\n        personal_notes = session.query(Note).filter(\n            Note.user_id == user_id).all()\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Authenticated user visits `/accounts/<any-user-id>/notes` -> 2. Query returns that user's notes (name collision lets attacker enumerate IDs) -> 3. Cross-user data exposure.\n**Mitigations:** None (route enforces authentication but not authorization/ownership).\n**Fix:** Enforce `user_id == current_user.id` (403/404 otherwise); scope queries to `current_user`.\n\n### routes/signup.py:15-18 — SQL injection on public `/signup` (password-hash exfiltration)\n**CWE:** CWE-89\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** HIGH\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact HIGH x Likelihood MEDIUM = HIGH (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `routes/signup.py:45` — `form.registration_code.data` (user-controlled, public `/signup` POST)\nTransform:  `routes/signup.py:46` — `validate_token(code, session)` interpolates `code` into `text(f\"...WHERE code = '{code}'\")`\nSink:       `routes/signup.py:15-18` — `session.execute(text(...))` runs raw SQL; `result.id` returns the first column, which a UNION payload can make a user's bcrypt hash\n\n```python\nresult = session.execute(\n    text(f\"\"\"\n        SELECT id, code FROM {RegistrationCode.__tablename__} WHERE code = '{code}'\n    \"\"\")).first()\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker POSTs `/signup` with `registration_code` = `' AND 1=0 UNION SELECT password, id FROM users LIMIT 1--` -> 2. Base query returns nothing, UNION returns `(bcrypt_hash, user_id)`; `result.id` = the hash -> 3. Collect hashes one request at a time, offline-crack bcrypt. (The line-52 `token.code != code` double-check blocks auth-bypass but not UNION exfiltration.)\n**Mitigations:** Partial — line 52 double-check blocks registration-bypass; `except OperationalError` suppresses error-based leakage. UNION exfiltration of the first column still works.\n**Fix:** Parameterize: `text(\"SELECT id, code FROM registration_codes WHERE code = :c\").bindparams(text('c', code))`. Never interpolate user input into `text()`.\n\n### routes/login.py:50-56 — Auth status / email disclosure on public `/is_logged_in`\n**CWE:** CWE-200\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** LOW\n**Likelihood:** HIGH\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood HIGH = LOW (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `routes/login.py:52-55` — response body built from `current_user.is_authenticated` and `current_user.email`\nTransform:  `routes/login.py:50` — `/is_logged_in` has no `@login_required` (public)\nSink:       `routes/login.py:52-55` — JSON response returns authenticated user's email + auth flag\n\n```python\n@app.route('/is_logged_in', methods=['GET'])\ndef logged_in():\n    return {\n        'is_logged_in': current_user.is_authenticated,\n        'username':\n        current_user.email if current_user.is_authenticated else '-'\n    }\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker (or a logged-in victim's context) GETs `/is_logged_in` -> 2. Response echoes the authenticated user's email address and auth status -> 3. Confirms an email is a registered/authenticated account (account enumeration aid).\n**Mitigations:** None (endpoint is public; returns email only for authenticated sessions).\n**Fix:** Enforce `@login_required`; return a generic boolean without the email, or remove the endpoint.\n\n### utils/profile_image.py:7 — SSRF / arbitrary file read via `urlopen(url)`\n**CWE:** CWE-918\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** HIGH\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact HIGH x Likelihood MEDIUM = HIGH (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `routes/account.py:60` — `get_base64_image_blob(form.url.data)` (user-provided URL via `/account/image` POST)\nTransform:  `utils/profile_image.py:11-12` — `get_base64_image_blob(url)` -> `download(url)`\nSink:       `utils/profile_image.py:7` — `urlopen(url)` with no scheme validation -> `file://` reads local files; `http://169.254.169.254/` SSRF to cloud metadata/internal services\n\n```python\ndef download(url: str) -> bytes:\n    with urlopen(url) as response:\n        return response.read()\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Authenticated user POSTs `/account/image` with `url=file:///etc/passwd` (or `http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/`) -> 2. `urlopen` fetches it (scheme unvalidated; `guess_type` only sets mimetype) -> 3. Base64 blob returned/stored -> arbitrary local file read or SSRF to internal endpoints.\n**Mitigations:** None (no URL scheme allowlist; only `guess_type` for mimetype).\n**Fix:** Allowlist URL schemes (`https` only); block `file://`, `gopher:`, internal IPs; fetch server-side with a bounded whitelist; never pass user-controlled URLs to `urlopen`.\n\n### routes/notes.py:41-48 — IDOR: delete any user's note by `note_id`\n**CWE:** CWE-284\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** MODERATE\n**Likelihood:** HIGH (note IDs are sequential auto-increment integers — `models/base_model.py:11`; `/notes/<id>/delete` is trivially enumerable)\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact MODERATE x Likelihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `routes/notes.py:39` — `<int:note_id>` from URL path\nTransform:  `routes/notes.py:44` — `session.get(Note, note_id)` — no `note.user_id == current_user.id` check\nSink:       `routes/notes.py:48` — `session.delete(note)` deletes another user's note\n\n```python\ndef delete_note(note_id: int):\n    with Session() as session:\n        note = session.get(Note, note_id)\n        if note is None:\n            flash('Note not found', 'warning')\n        else:\n            session.delete(note)\n            session.commit()\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Authenticated user POSTs `/notes/<any-note-id>/delete` -> 2. Server loads and deletes the note regardless of owner -> 3. Destruction of other users' notes (data tampering).\n**Mitigations:** None (enforces authentication, not ownership).\n**Fix:** Check `note.user_id == current_user.id` before deleting (404 otherwise); scope to `current_user`.\n\n### db_seed.py:9 — Hardcoded, README-published registration code\n**CWE:** CWE-259\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** LOW\n**Likelihood:** HIGH\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood HIGH = LOW (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `db_seed.py:9` — static registration code literal `'a36e990b-0024-4d55-b74a-f8d7528e1764'`\nTransform:  `db_seed.py:10` — seeded into `RegistrationCode` table at startup (`setup_db()`, called from `app.py:21` on fresh DB)\nSink:       `db_seed.py:9` — published verbatim in `README.md` (\"use the leaked invite code ...\")\n\n```python\nif session.query(RegistrationCode).count() == 0:\n    static_code = 'a36e990b-0024-4d55-b74a-f8d7528e1764'\n    session.add(RegistrationCode(static_code))\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker reads the code from the public README -> 2. Uses it on `/signup` to create an account -> 3. Unauthorized account creation (bypasses invite generation).\n**Mitigations:** None (code is hardcoded and publicly documented).\n**Fix:** Generate registration codes at runtime; never hardcode or publish invite codes.\n\n### db_seed.py:18-19 — Admin account with weak, known password (`'admin'`)\n**CWE:** CWE-259\n**Reachability:** CONDITIONAL\n**Impact:** HIGH\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact HIGH x Likelihood MEDIUM = HIGH (CONDITIONAL)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `db_seed.py:18-19` — admin account seeded with `hashpw(b'admin', gensalt())` (password is literally `'admin'`)\nTransform:  `db_seed.py:22` — admin (`is_admin=True`) created on fresh DB (`User.count() == 0`)\nSink:       login (`routes/login.py:32`) — `bcrypt.checkpw` verifies against the cracked hash\n\n```python\nadmin = User('admin@evfa.com',\n             hashpw(b'admin', gensalt()).decode(), True)\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. On a freshly-seeded DB, admin's bcrypt hash corresponds to the password `'admin'` -> 2. Attacker obtains the hash (e.g., via the `/signup` SQLi exfiltration) -> 3. `'admin'` cracks in seconds; logs in as admin (privilege escalation).\n**Mitigations:** Password is bcrypt-hashed (not plaintext), but `'admin'` is a top-common password, cracked instantly offline.\n**Fix:** Do not ship predefined admin accounts with weak passwords; force password change on first login; use strong randomly-generated seeds.\n\n### forms/account_form.py:4 + routes/account.py:81 — Mass-assignment → privilege escalation (`is_admin`)\n**CWE:** CWE-284\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** HIGH\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact HIGH x Likelihood MEDIUM = HIGH (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `forms/account_form.py:4` — `is_admin = BooleanField('Is Admin')` (field present in submitted form)\nTransform:  `routes/account.py:81` — `current_user.__dict__.update(form.data)` copies ALL form fields onto the user object\nSink:       `routes/account.py:84` — `session.commit()` persists `is_admin` (and `password`/`email`) to the DB\n\n```python\ncurrent_user.__dict__.update(form.data)\nsession.commit()\n```\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Authenticated user POSTs `/account` with `is_admin=true` (and/or `password=<hash>`) -> 2. `form.data` includes `is_admin` -> 3. `current_user.__dict__.update` sets `is_admin=True`, `session.commit()` promotes the account to admin (privilege escalation).\n**Mitigations:** `email` change is guarded (line 78); `is_admin`/`password` are not (unchecked mass-assignment).\n**Fix:** Do not map form data onto ORM objects wholesale. Assign only whitelisted fields (`email`/`password` via `hashpw`); never copy `is_admin` or other privileged columns from form input.\n\n### All state-changing POST routes — CSRF (no token / SameSite hardening)\n**CWE:** CWE-352\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** MODERATE\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact MODERATE x Likelihood MEDIUM = MEDIUM (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nTransform: State-changing POST endpoints — `/account` (account.py:73), `/account/image` (account.py:93), `/notes` (notes.py:17), `/notes/<id>/delete` (notes.py:39), `/signup` (signup.py:33), `/registration-codes` (registration_codes.py:26) — none implement a CSRF token / `CSRFProtect` / `SameSite` cookie hardening.\nSink: Cross-origin forged request from an attacker-controlled page -> server processes the victim's authenticated session.\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker serves a page that auto-POSTs to `/account` with `is_admin=true` (mass-assignment) or `/account/image` with `url=file:///...` (SSRF) -> 2. Browser sends the victim's authenticated session cookies -> 3. Victim's account is escalated to admin / SSRF triggered without consent (also forces note deletion, password change).\n\n**Mitigations:** None (no CSRF token; session cookies lack `SameSite` hardening).\n**Fix:** Apply `flask_wtf.csrf.csrfProtect`; set `SameSite=Lax/Strict` session cookies; verify origin/`Referer` on state-changing POSTs; require anti-CSRF tokens in forms.\n\n### models/__init__.py:14 — SQL `echo=True` logs sensitive queries to server logs\n**CWE:** CWE-200\n**Reachability:** ACTIVE\n**Impact:** LOW\n**Likelihood:** LOW\n**Confidence:** CONFIRMED\n**Severity:** Impact LOW x Likelihood LOW = LOW (ACTIVE)\n\n**Data flow:**\nSource:     `models/__init__.py:14` — `create_engine('sqlite:///' + ..., echo=True)`\nTransform:  `echo=True` logs every executed SQL statement **including bound parameters** to console/server logs\nSink:       server logs (uwsgi stdout) — contain user emails and bcrypt password hashes\n\n**Exploit:** 1. Attacker obtains server logs (log files, uwsgi stdout, centralized logging) -> 2. Reads logged SQL with bound params -> 3. Exposes user emails and bcrypt password hashes.\n\n**Mitigations:** None (`echo` left enabled).\n**Fix:** Set `echo=False` in production; never log query parameters containing credentials.\n\n## Dependency scan\nNo `DIFF_SCOPE.md` present — scanned the whole project (no diff-scoping). Grype baseline + OSV-Scanner (PyPI, `requirements.txt`).\n\n**Grype baseline** (pre-processing):\n- `werkzeug@3.1.5` → CVE-2026-27199 (GHSA-29vq-49wr-vm6x), Medium, CWE-67, fixed in 3.1.6.\n\n**OSV-Scanner** (whole-project):\n| Package | Version | CVE / PYSEC | Severity (CVSS) | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| click | 8.1.7 | PYSEC-2026-2132 (CVE-2026-7246) — command injection in `click.edit()` | High (7.2) | 8.3.3 |\n| flask | 3.1.1 | PYSEC-2026-2151 | Medium (4.3) | 3.1.3 |\n| werkzeug | 3.1.5 | PYSEC-2026-2320 | Medium (6.3) | 3.1.6 |\n\n**Diff (baseline → OSV-Scanner):** `click` (High) and `flask` (Medium) are new vs the grype baseline; `werkzeug` carries a second, distinct CVE (OSV: PYSEC-2026-2320 vs grype: CVE-2026-27199). All three are upstream dependencies (Flask → click; Flask/Werkzeug).\n**Note:** `click` command injection is confined to `click.edit()` (interactive editor), which this app does not call — so actual exploitability is low despite the High CVSS. `flask`/`werkzeug` vulns are library-level (patch to update).\n**Fix:** Pin `click>=8.3.3`, `flask>=3.1.3`, `werkzeug>=3.1.6`; re-audit.\n\n## Summary tables\n\n### Table 1 — All findings by severity\n| # | Location | CWE | Reachability | Severity |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | app.py:11 | CWE-259 (hardcoded secret) | ACTIVE | CRITICAL |\n| 2 | app.py:31-33 | CWE-94 (SSTI/RCE) | ACTIVE | CRITICAL |\n| 3 | account.py:118 | CWE-502 (pickle.loads RCE) | ACTIVE | CRITICAL |\n| 4 | account.py:33 | CWE-89 (SQLi) | ACTIVE | HIGH |\n| 5 | signup.py:15-18 | CWE-89 (SQLi, public /signup) | ACTIVE | HIGH |\n| 6 | profile_image.py:7 | CWE-918 (SSRF/file://) | ACTIVE | HIGH |\n| 7 | db_seed.py:18-19 | CWE-259 (weak admin password) | CONDITIONAL | HIGH |\n| 8 | account_form.py:4 + account.py:81 | CWE-284 (mass-assignment → admin) | ACTIVE | HIGH |\n| 9 | account.py:43-46 | CWE-284 (IDOR read notes) | ACTIVE | MEDIUM |\n| 10 | notes.py:41-48 | CWE-284 (IDOR delete notes) | ACTIVE | MEDIUM |\n| 11 | routes/* (all POST) | CWE-352 (CSRF) | ACTIVE | MEDIUM |\n| 12 | login.py:50-56 | CWE-200 (email/auth disclosure) | ACTIVE | LOW |\n| 13 | db_seed.py:9 | CWE-259 (hardcoded invite code) | ACTIVE | LOW |\n| 14 | models/__init__.py:14 | CWE-200 (SQL echo logs) | ACTIVE | LOW |\n\n**Totals:** CRITICAL 3, HIGH 5, MEDIUM 3, LOW 3 (14 findings).\n\n### Table 2 — Findings by vulnerability type\n| Type | Findings | Count |\n|---|---|---|\n| SQL Injection (CWE-89) | #4, #5 | 2 |\n| Server-Side Template Injection / RCE (CWE-94) | #2 | 1 |\n| Insecure Deserialization / RCE (CWE-502) | #3 | 1 |\n| SSRF / Arbitrary File Read (CWE-918) | #6 | 1 |\n| Broken Access Control — IDOR (CWE-284) | #9, #10 | 2 |\n| Broken Access Control — Mass-assignment / Privilege Escalation (CWE-284) | #8 | 1 |\n| Cross-Site Request Forgery (CWE-352) | #11 | 1 |\n| Hardcoded Credentials / Secrets (CWE-259) | #1, #7, #13 | 3 |\n| Information Exposure (CWE-200) | #12, #14 | 2 |\n\n### Top risks (active, highest priority)\n1. **`account.py:118` pickle.loads RCE** — unauthenticated (via `before_request`), no auth/session needed → full server compromise. **Fix:** never `pickle.loads`; validate/parse JSON.\n2. **`app.py:31-33` SSTI/RCE** — `render_template_string(request.path)` in the 404 handler → attacker-controlled template → RCE. **Fix:** serve a static 404 page; never `render_template_string` on user input.\n3. **`app.py:11` hardcoded `secret_key`** — session forgery (sign any session, forge admin). **Fix:** read from env/secret manager.\n4. **`account.py:81` mass-assignment → `is_admin`** — authenticated admin escalation (unlocks the admin-only `/registration-codes` gate). **Fix:** whitelist fields; never `__dict__.update(form.data)`.\n5. **`account.py:33` / `signup.py:17` SQLi** — parameterize `text()`; don't interpolate.\n\n### Remediation roadmap (prioritized)\n**P0 — Fix now (RCE / full compromise):**\n- `account.py:118` — replace `pickle.loads(cookie)` with a validated format (e.g., HMAC-signed JSON); run deserialization only on trusted data.\n- `app.py:31-33` — return a static 404; remove `render_template_string`.\n- `app.py:11` — move `secret_key` to an environment variable / secrets store.\n\n**P1 — Fix soon (authn/authz / data):**\n- `account.py:33` + `signup.py:17` — parameterize all SQL (bind params); never `text(f\"...{var}...\")`.\n- `account_form.py:4` + `account.py:81` — assign only whitelisted fields (`email`, bcrypt'd `password`); never copy `is_admin`/`password` from `form.data`.\n- `profile_image.py:7` — allowlist URL scheme (https only), block `file://`/internal IPs; fetch server-side.\n- `notes.py:41-48` + `account.py:43-46` — enforce `owner == current_user.id` (404/403 otherwise); IDs are sequential (enumerable).\n- `db_seed.py:18-19` — remove the seeded admin account with password `'admin'` (crackable); force password reset on first login.\n\n**P2 — Harden:**\n- Add CSRF protection (`CSRFProtect` / `SameSite` cookies) to all state-changing POSTs.\n- `db_seed.py:9` — stop hardcoding/publishing invite codes; generate at runtime.\n- `models/__init__.py:14` — set `echo=False`; never log query parameters.\n- `login.py:50-56` — remove email/auth disclosure from `/is_logged_in` (or gate it).\n\n**P3 — Supply chain:**\n- Upgrade `click>=8.3.3`, `flask>=3.1.3`, `werkzeug>=3.1.6`; re-audit on version changes.\n\n## Pre-processing artifacts\n- SBOM available: `.security-output/sbom.cyclonedx.json` (used in step 7).\n- Grype results present: `.security-output/grype-results.json` (summarized above).\n- `DIFF_SCOPE.md`: not present — no diff-scoping; all files reviewed per step 6 priority.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":512,"totalLines":512,"truncated":false}},"title":".security-output/SEC_ASSESSMENT_Ornith_1_5_35B_A3B_MLX_4bit.md","time":{"start":1788165758959,"end":1788165758966}},"id":"prt_056fc1fe9001rSrCHCFDnOuYk7","sessionID":"ses_fa923204fffeJOVYIIzNA2JDJK","messageID":"msg_056fbcab0001loBhxO93b2gbVw"}}
